cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work or its verification package, please cite the following entry."
title: "A Shift Law for Central Gaps of Gaussian Binomial Coefficients"
authors:
  - family-names: Hu
    given-names: Gerald W.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/GeWoHu/gaussian-shift-law"
abstract: >-
  Public research preprint (not peer reviewed) proving that the central gap of
  the Gaussian binomial coefficient [l+6 choose 6]_q satisfies the shift law
  g_6(l) = g_6(l-15) for every odd integer l >= 17, with sharp thresholds
  l_0(6,8)=14, l_0(6,12)=20, l_0(6,16)=26, a complete zero classification, and
  a counterexample to universal central dominance at (b,k)=(6,24). Includes a
  complete exact-integer machine-verification package with independent
  re-certification of all tail obligations.
keywords:
  - Gaussian binomial coefficients
  - q-binomial coefficients
  - unimodality
  - central gap
  - computer verification
license: MIT
license-manuscript: CC0-1.0
